## Emergency Kill-Switch Protocol

If an unexpected exception spike or backend latency surge is detected, the feature can be globally deactivated in under 60 seconds without an app store submission:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Ops as Mobile Ops Engineer
    participant Unleash as Unleash Console
    participant Proxy as Unleash Proxy Edge
    participant App as Mobile App (unleash-proxy-client)

    Ops->>Unleash: Toggle Flag OFF in Production
    Unleash->>Proxy: Webhook syncs state (Instant)
    App->>Proxy: Polling query /proxy (within 15s)
    Proxy-->>App: Returns toggle payload (flag: false)
    App->>App: Re-evaluates UI & falls back to legacy path
```

1. **Step 1: Detection:** Datadog Mobile RUM triggers a P1 alert (Crash-free users drop below 99.8% or API 5xx rate exceeds 1%).
2. **Step 2: Deactivation:** Engineer toggles the flag to **OFF** in the Unleash Admin Console.
3. **Step 3: Edge Propagation:** Unleash Edge/Proxy updates immediately via push or within 15 seconds.
4. **Step 4: Client Fast-Fail:** Active client applications fetch the updated state on the next 15s poll or upon foregrounding, immediately swapping back to the stable legacy code path.

