## Architectural Non-Negotiables & Prohibitions

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">UNLEASH ARCHITECTURAL ENFORCEMENTS</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1. No Direct Core Connections:</strong> Mobile binaries must NEVER connect directly to the core Unleash Server. All traffic must route through the Unleash Proxy. PRs containing core Unleash admin URLs are blocked by CI.</li>
    <li><strong>2. No Blocking App Launch:</strong> Never block app cold-start waiting for an Unleash HTTP response. Always initialize with synchronous cached values from local storage (MMKV / EncryptedSharedPreferences / Keychain).</li>
    <li><strong>3. Mandatory Fallback Defaults:</strong> Every <code>isEnabled()</code> call must specify an explicit, safe fallback boolean to ensure graceful degradation when offline.</li>
    <li><strong>4. Stickiness Must Be Set to `userId`:</strong> Never use <code>random</code> stickiness in mobile rollouts, as user state would flip between app restarts.</li>
    <li><strong>5. Standardized Flag Naming:</strong> Flags must follow the strict schema: <code>mobile.[platform].[domain].[feature_name]</code> (e.g., <code>mobile.all.checkout.one_click_pay</code>).</li>
  </ul>
